orm=\"translate(111.40625 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_11\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(323.752988 37.368) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-85\" transform=\"translate(46.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(111.90625 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p686c9b05a4\"><rect x=\"45.676437\" y=\"10.824\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"127.512\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Value to Redline vs price ($M)","note":null},"answer":"<p>60% of fees come from rivals and half of them leave: Haulmark loses 30% of its revenue. Standalone value falls to $84M.</p> <p>Total value: $84M + $64M = <b>$148M</b>, below the $150M price. With fewer carriers, the app may also attract fewer shippers, so it could fall further.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> buying Haulmark damages the very thing that makes it valuable: its neutrality.</p>"},{"q":"How else could Redline fill its empty return trips?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li><b>Commercial partnership</b> with Haulmark: guaranteed volume on Redline's routes in return for first look at return loads. If it captures 75% of the benefit, that's ~$6M a year, worth about $48M at 8×, for no money up front. Buying is worth about −$2M after the price</li> <li>Use several freight apps at once</li><li>Sign direct contracts with shippers on its main return lanes</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Don't buy Haulmark. On paper it is worth $184M to Redline, but about 60% of its fees come from Redline's rivals, and if half of them leave, the value falls to about $148M, below the $150M price. Instead, agree a partnership that gives Redline first access to return loads on its routes, which captures most of the ~$8M a year benefit without the purchase. Risk: a rival could buy Haulmark, so include a right to bid in the partnership. Next step: approach Haulmark with a volume-for-priority proposal.","great":["Values the deal before and after customer reactions","Spots that neutrality is the asset","Shows the deal flips from positive to negative","Finds a way to get the benefit without buying"],"id":66,"slug":"haulmark"}